            "question": {
              "question": {
                "content": "A microbiologist is studying the growth of a specific bacterial strain in a nutrient-rich environment. They observe that the bacterial population doubles every hour. If the initial population at the start of the experiment ($t=0$ hours) is 100 bacteria, write an expression representing the total number of bacteria, $N$, after $t$ hours. Assume $t$ is a non-negative integer.\n\nYour expression should use $t$ as the variable.\n$N = $ [[\u2603 expression 1]]",
                "images": {},
                "widgets": {
                  "expression 1": {
                    "type": "expression",
                    "options": {
                      "buttonsVisible": "never",
                      "functions": [
                        "f",
                        "g",
